{
  "_comment": "KrashiMitra crop-type registry. It answers one question: how often does a farmer re-decide the sale of this crop? That cadence — not the botanical family — is what the /bhav layout should follow. Wheat is sold once a season against MSP; tomato is re-decided every morning against arrivals. Read live and cached by mtime (see services/crop_types.py), so adding a crop is a JSON edit, never a deploy. Keys are /bhav URL slugs, lowercase, exactly as they appear in the path.",

  "_resolution_order": "1) crops{} exact slug  2) rules[] first keyword match, in listed order  3) default. Never raises, always returns a known type — an unclassified commodity must render exactly as it does today.",

  "default": "staple",

  "types": {
    "perishable": {
      "hi": "जल्दी खराब होने वाली",
      "layout": "daily",
      "cadence_days": 1,
      "why": "Sells within days of harvest, no holding option. Price moves with आवक (arrivals) far more than with season. The page must lead with direction and freshness — कल से कितना, 7-day range, arrivals — because the number alone is stale by evening."
    },
    "storable": {
      "hi": "भंडारण योग्य",
      "layout": "holding",
      "cadence_days": 7,
      "why": "Can go to cold storage, so the real question is not 'what is the price' but 'sell now or hold'. The page must carry seasonality, holding cost and cold-store options alongside the number."
    },
    "staple": {
      "hi": "मुख्य फसल",
      "layout": "season",
      "cadence_days": 90,
      "why": "Sold once or twice a marketing season, usually against MSP. Procurement centre, MSP gap and net-price-after-transport matter; day-over-day movement mostly does not. This is today's layout and the safe default."
    }
  },

